LABRECORDER SETUP
=================

Download: https://github.com/labstreaminglayer/App-LabRecorder/releases

Workflow
--------
  1. Start BlueMuse or muselsl so the Muse EEG stream is visible on LSL.
  2. Open LabRecorder.
  3. In the "Record from streams" list you should see at minimum:
       type=EEG   (Muse 2, 4 ch, ~256 Hz)
     After PsychoPy starts you will also see:
       type=Markers  (SandhiMarkers, integer event codes)
  4. Set the output directory and filename before pressing Start.
     Recommended naming: <participant_id>_<date>_sandhi.xdf
  5. Press "Start" — confirm the file size counter begins incrementing.
  6. Launch the experiment via:  python run_experiment.py
  7. After the experiment ends, press "Stop" in LabRecorder and verify
     the .xdf file exists and is non-zero in size.

Marker stream timing note
-------------------------
  The 'SandhiMarkers' LSL stream is created by PsychoPy when the experiment
  script starts. LabRecorder will auto-detect it and begin recording markers
  from that point. No manual action is needed — LabRecorder monitors for
  new streams during a session. However, starting LabRecorder BEFORE PsychoPy
  ensures the EEG baseline (pre-experiment) is captured as well.

XDF analysis
------------
  See software/matlab.md for EEGLab + xdf-EEGLAB plugin instructions.
  For Python-based analysis, use MNE-Python with the pyxdf loader:
    pip install mne pyxdf
